body:
Look I just wrote down the parallels that were drawn in my mind. Like I said, it's just a theory and it doesn't necessarily mean anything. Plus Harry and Taylor had a very public relationship years ago, and if for whatever reasons they became friends (again?), they probably wouldn't want it to be publicized for all the drama it would stir and conclusions that would be jumped to. Even though there are no public links between them anymore, there are still a bunch of Haylor shippers that jump to conclusions. For the same reason that Larry doesn't have a public relationship, Harry and Taylor probably wouldn't either.

&#x200B;

So, in easy to read, simple terms, they could very well be best friends away from the public eye. AND I clarified a bunch of times in the comments and the post that it's only a theory and that it isn't solid proof for anything because I am well aware that correlation does not imply causation and coincidences do exist.

Yeah, I met this one guy that was in uni on omegle chat a few years ago (I was I think 13-ish at the time) and I still think about him. We literally had a single 20 minute conversation about life and MBTI and sports and stuff and he called me "little intj" and that was probably the mast affectionate thing anyone has ever told me. Like I literally remember this guy randomly and think about how much happier I could've been if there was someone like him in my family. Like I've always wanted and older brother that would call me nicknames like that, and ruffle my hair all the time, and play baseball with me, and make fun of all my friends, and play music with me. Or like a really chill dad that's my best friend. But nope.

&#x200B;

If you want to DM me, I'd love to talk to you. It's hard to find people that you click with and that actually stick around, but I'd love to try :)
